# Add a new page under `(site)`

Use this checklist when introducing a route like `/menu`: URL, shell colour wipe, header nav, gated body reveal, optional CTA.

## 1. Route files

Create a segment under `app/(site)/`:

- `page.tsx` - thin server component only: pass-through `main` shell + composes one client content module.

```tsx
// app/(site)/example/page.tsx
import { ExampleContent } from "./example-content";

export default function ExamplePage() {
  return (
    <main
      id="main-content"
      tabIndex={-1}
      className="relative isolate flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden bg-transparent"
    >
      <ExampleContent />
    </main>
  );
}
```

- `*-content.tsx` - `"use client"`; composes the shared placeholder / content component.

For placeholders, use `app/(site)/_components/site-placeholder-content.tsx`. The shell (`SiteChrome`) controls `isContentRevealed`, so page content can fade in exactly when the wipe peels away.

Important: page content reveal is a **fade only**. Do not add swipe/slide (`x`/`y`) or blur unless product asks.

## 2. Register the wipe/backdrop colour

Edit `lib/site-route-theme.ts`: add `{ match: "/example", palette: { css: "var(--color-bom-…)", hex: "#…" } }`.

Pick tokens from `@theme inline` in `app/globals.css` (`--color-bom-*`). `hex` must match the CSS token so Framer can interpolate the overlay.

Order matters (first matching prefix wins). Put **specific** paths before broader ones if needed.

Default palette is applied when pathname does not match any entry (`getSitePalette`).

## 3. Header link (optional)

`components/header/site-header.tsx`: add `<Link href="/example">…</Link>` beside existing nav entries.

Deferred navigation intercepts internal **same-origin** `<a href>` clicks at the `(site)` root; no extra wiring per route.

## 4. Timing (global)

Tune in `lib/site-page-transition-timing.ts`:

- Overlay: `coverDurationS`, `briefHoldS`, `revealSpring`, etc.
- Pre-navigation outgoing fade delay: **`contentExitDurationS`** (`SiteChrome` `setTimeout` + motion).
- Incoming body fade: `SiteChrome` toggles `isContentRevealed` through `SitePageTransitionProvider` at peel time.

Avoid animating **`exit`** expecting it to control “leave” timing: **`app/(site)/template.tsx` remounts every navigation**. Outgoing fades are driven by **`components/site/site-chrome.tsx`** (deferred link handler + keyed `AnimatePresence`).

## 5. Buttons (placeholder / CTAs)

Use `Button` from `components/ui/button.tsx`: **`variant="bomPill"`** + **`size="bomPill"`** to match signup (Stay in the loop). Mirror Klaviyo’s layout classes (`w-full lg:w-auto …`, `font-sans font-medium antialiased`).

Prefer **`asChild`** + `<Link>` with label wrapped in `<span>`.

- Use a BOM fill that **contrasts** the page wipe colour (avoid same-as-background pills).
- **No custom hover colours** unless product asks (`hover:bg-*` / `hover:text-*` on these CTAs is intentionally omitted).

## 6. Sanity check

After adding a route:

- `npm run build`
- Navigate from header/links: current view should stay frozen, destination colour should cover, route should swap behind the full cover, then the overlay should peel while content fades in.
